{"study_accession":"PRJNA1222890","secondary_study_accession":"SRP563587","title":"Enhanced Antitumoral Activity of the Academic CAR-T ARI0002h Against Normal and Low BCMA Expressing Myeloma Cells After Incorporating a Transmembrane CD28 Domain","description":"BCMA is the main target for CAR-T cells in multiple myeloma (MM), demonstrating promising outcomes. However, unlike what happens with CART19 in lymphoblastic leukemia and non-hodgkin lymphoma, a high proportion of patients will relapse after CART BCMA therapy due to insufficient antigen expression, low CAR-T cell persistence and/or T-cell exhaustion. CD28 transmembrane domains (CD28-TMD) in CAR receptors promote dimerization with CD28, forming CAR-CD28 heterodimers that enhance sensitivity to low-abundance antigens. In other B cell malignancies, second-generation anti-CD19 4-1BB CARs with CD28-TMD have shown high efficacy and a favorable toxicity profile. We have developed a second-generation CD8α-TMD BCMA-4-1BBζ CAR-T product, ARI0002h (ARI2h; cesni-cel) for patients with relapsed/refractory MM. We hypothesized that replacing the TMD of ARI0002h with a CD28-TMD could increase efficacy and reduce tumor escape while maintaining a tolerable toxicity profile. We generated CAR-T cells using T-cells isolated from buffy coats and evaluated the efficacy and fitness of CAR-Ts at day 8-10 of expansion against several MM cell lines. In vitro analyses included cytotoxicity, proliferation, cytokine secretion, T-cell subset markers, activation and exhaustion profiling, metabolomic assays, and RNA-seq after multiple tumor challenges. In in vivo xenograft studies using NSG mice, with tumor cells expressing GFP-ffLuc, disease progression was monitored weekly via bioluminescence imaging. Overall design: CAR-T cells were co-cultured with ARP-1 GFP+ target cells at a 1:2 E:T for 48 hours, after which the remaining CAR-T cells were rechallenged with fresh target cells under identical conditions. This process was repeated for up to four rounds. Post-rechallenge, CD8+ CAR-T cells were isolated using a magnetic bead-based CD8 Positive Selection Kit (EasySep).","pubmed":"41775430","geo_series":"","n_samples":8,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN46796831","study_accession":"PRJNA1222890","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"CD8+ CAR-T cell, TM28, Donor 24","description":"CD8+ CAR-T cell, TM28, Donor 24","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8791290","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-03-22","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral blood"],["tissue","Peripheral blood"],["cell_type","CD8+ T cells"],["genotype","CD28 domain"],["treatment","ARP-1 stimulated"],["batch","September 11th 2024"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR32326114","experiment_accession":"SRX27661075","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq X Plus","read_count":32491244,"base_count":9747373200,"first_public":"2026-03-22","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq X Plus sequencing: GSM8791290: CD8+ CAR-T cell, TM28, Donor 24 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN46796832","study_accession":"PRJNA1222890","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"CD8+ CAR-T cell, ARI2, Donor 24","description":"CD8+ CAR-T cell, ARI2, Donor 24","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8791289","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-03-22","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral blood"],["tissue","Peripheral blood"],["cell_type","CD8+ T cells"],["genotype","CD8 alpha domain"],["treatment","ARP-1 stimulated"],["batch","September 11th 2024"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR32326115","experiment_accession":"SRX27661074","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq X Plus","read_count":32828981,"base_count":9848694300,"first_public":"2026-03-22","experiment_titl